From: hui CI <noreply@farna.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] window: brace-init the title bar's CrossAlign

Clang does not implement P0960 (aggregate parenthesized initialization) in
Objective-C++ mode, so every AppKit translation unit that includes this header
fails with "no matching conversion for functional-style cast". Brace
initialization means the same thing here and works in every language mode.

Applies on top of the pinned HuxerUI commit; harmless on Linux and Windows,
where the functional cast does compile.

diff --git a/include/huxerui/window.h b/include/huxerui/window.h
--- a/include/huxerui/window.h
+++ b/include/huxerui/window.h
@@ -261,7 +261,7 @@ class WindowTitleBar final : public Layout<WindowTitleBar> {
 public:
   /// Constructs a title bar from an existing child collection.
   explicit WindowTitleBar(std::vector<View> children) : Layout(std::move(children)) {
-    this->ApplyModifiers(WindowDragRegion{}, CrossAlign(CrossAxisAlignment::Center));
+    this->ApplyModifiers(WindowDragRegion{}, CrossAlign{CrossAxisAlignment::Center});
   }
 
   /// Constructs a title bar from ordinary View children.
